== S1. Decode: E = 6 B(M+2,T+2) is the Polya(2,2) sequence law ==
  E(T,M)=6B(M+2,T+2)=Polya(2,2) law; split identity; 6*H_3=11; P1-integrated beta(2,2) bound 17/2; beta(1,2) bound 16/3
  root rays 3 (E) and 2 (W); leaf masses 2 (E) and 1 (W); ord_9(2)=6, ord_9(4)=3; 2^6/3 = 21.33 < 22
  controls: E(27)=1/21296186450 at (L,K)=(40,8); 53,113 -> (1,3); 111 -> (23,7); 155 -> (29,8)
== S2. Theorem A mechanism: split arrays are Hausdorff moment arrays ==
  six random discrete mixtures: positivity, split, (-Delta)^L row formula, exact fibre remainders; non-monotone row gives w(2,0)<0; atom at r=1 gives root-row defect = atom mass
