== S4. Ascending shadows force non-uniformity of every supersolution ==
  2^(l+1)-1 -> 2*3^l-1 in l U-steps of valuation 1, l<=60; ratio (2*3^l-1)/(2^(l+1)-1) -> (3/2)^l
  (-17)-cycle word (1,1,1,2,1,1,4): shadows 2^(11m)t-17 climb to 3^(7m)t-17 (t even) (m<=3, t in 2..10); multiplier 3^7/2^11 = 1.0679
== S5. Leaf section tower: least predecessor divisible by 3^j ==
  j=1: sup_(v<2e5) rho_j(v)/v = 21.333332 at v=199999; bound 2^(2*3^j)/3 = 21.3333
  j=2: sup_(v<2e5) rho_j(v)/v = 87381.333332 at v=199963; bound 2^(2*3^j)/3 = 87381.3
  j=3: sup_(v<2e5) rho_j(v)/v = 6004799503160661.000000 at v=199909; bound 2^(2*3^j)/3 = 6.0048e+15
  table a_0(v mod 9) = {1:6,2:5,4:4,5:1,7:2,8:3}; unit-predecessor exponents {1:2,2:1,4:2,5:3,7:4,8:1} (bound 16/3); leaf predecessors of v are S^(3t) rho_1(v)
